## Code Comments

### When to Comment

**Do Comment:**

- Complex algorithms
- Non-obvious business logic
- Workarounds for bugs
- Performance optimizations
- Security considerations
- Public APIs (JSDoc)

**Don't Comment:**

- Obvious code
- What the code does (should be self-evident)
- Commented-out code (use git history)
- Redundant information

### Comment Style

```typescript
// Good: Explains WHY
// Use exponential backoff to avoid overwhelming the server during reconnection storms
await retry(connect, { maxAttempts: 3, backoff: 'exponential' });

// Bad: Explains WHAT (obvious from code)
// Retry the connection 3 times
await retry(connect, { maxAttempts: 3 });
```

### TODO Comments

Use standardized TODO format:

```typescript
// TODO(username): Add support for custom MCP transports
// TODO: Implement thought export to PDF
// FIXME: Handle race condition in tree refresh
// HACK: Temporary workaround for VS Code API bug (#12345)
```

## Inline Documentation

### Type Definitions

Document complex types:

```typescript
/**
 * Represents the state of an MCP connection.
 *
 * @property status - Current connection status
 * @property lastConnected - Timestamp of last successful connection (ISO 8601)
 * @property retryCount - Number of reconnection attempts
 */
interface ConnectionState {
  status: 'connected' | 'disconnected' | 'connecting' | 'error';
  lastConnected?: string;
  retryCount: number;
}
```

### Constants

```typescript
/**
 * Maximum number of thoughts to keep in memory before archiving.
 * Prevents memory issues with long-running thinking sessions.
 */
const MAX_THOUGHT_HISTORY = 1000;
```

### Configuration

Document configuration options in package.json:

```json
{
  "contributes": {
    "configuration": {
      "properties": {
        "sequential-thinking-vis.autoConnect": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Automatically connect to MCP server on startup. Disable if you prefer manual connection control. See [documentation](https://example.com/docs) for details."
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

